    "mathematical_proof": "MATHEMATICAL PROOF OF CLASSIFICATION HYSTERESIS:\nLet C_t be close price, E_50(t) be EMA50, and E_200(t) be EMA200 at bar t.\nDefinition of states:\n  S_t = BULLISH   iff (C_t > E_50(t)) AND (E_50(t) > E_200(t))\n  S_t = BEARISH   iff (C_t < E_50(t)) AND (E_50(t) < E_200(t))\n  S_t = SIDEWAYS  otherwise.\n\nConsider a bar t where S_t = BULLISH. Hence E_50(t) - E_200(t) > 0 and C_t > E_50(t).\nFor a direct transition S_{t+1} = BEARISH in a single 15m bar, we require:\n  1. C_{t+1} < E_50(t+1)\n  2. E_50(t+1) < E_200(t+1)\n\nBecause E_50 and E_200 are updated via exponential smoothing:\n  E_50(t+1) - E_200(t+1) = (E_50(t) - E_200(t)) + (alpha_50 - alpha_200)*C_{t+1} - alpha_50*E_50(t) + alpha_200*E_200(t).\nWith alpha_50 = 2/51 ~ 0.0392 and alpha_200 = 2/201 ~ 0.00995, alpha_50 - alpha_200 ~ 0.0293.\nIn an established trend, E_50(t) exceeds E_200(t) by delta >> 0 (typically 1-5% of price, or $500-$3,000 on BTC).\nEven during an extreme 15m flash crash where C_{t+1} falls far below E_50(t+1), the single-bar adjustment to E_50 - E_200\nis bounded by ~0.0293 * (C_{t+1} - E_50(t)), which cannot bridge delta in a single bar.\nTherefore, on the breakdown bar t+1, condition (1) C_{t+1} < E_50(t+1) holds, but condition (2) FAILS (E_50(t+1) > E_200(t+1) persists).\nBy definition, this intermediate topological region maps strictly to SIDEWAYS_RANGE.\nDirect transitions are mathematically impossible except in the singular boundary case where |E_50(t) - E_200(t)| < epsilon\n(within $1-3) at the precise moment price crosses both EMAs.",
    "auditor_conclusion": "AUDIT VERDICT: The reported near-zero direct transition rate (0.08% BULL->BEAR, 0.11% BEAR->BULL) is primarily Category C (Combined Effect, predominantly an algorithmic classification artifact). The dual-indicator classification creates a topological hysteresis manifold in feature space that forces price through the complement region (SIDEWAYS_RANGE). Single-indicator null models demonstrate hundreds of direct flips (753 transitions). This property is an algorithmic guarantee of the classifier geometry, NOT a discovery of market dynamics."
  },
